    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Check NWS updates here At 1028 PM CDT/928 PM MDT/, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 17 miles south of Carson, or 33 miles northeast of Lemmon, moving southeast at 35 mph. HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and penny size hail. SOURCE...Radar indicated. IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is possible. Locations impacted include... Standing Rock.",
